225 937 686 (        1.1 Introduction to CP/M 3) 686 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
375 1055 1733 (CP/M 3 provides an environment for program development and execution on computer) 1733 SB
225 1115 1871 (systems that use the Intel 8080, 8085, -or ZBO microprocessor chip.    CP/M 3 provides rapid) 1871 SB
225 1174 1935 (access to data and programs through a file structure that supports dynamic allocation of space for) 1935 SB
225 1233 691 (sequential and random access files.) 691 SB
375 1351 1635 (CP/M 3 supports a maximum of sixteen logical floppy or hard disks with a storage) 1635 SB
225 1410 1912 (capacity of up to 512 megabytes each.   The maximum file size supported is 32 megabytes.  You) 1912 SB
225 1470 1773 (can configure the number of directory entries and block size to satisfy various user needs.) 1773 SB
375 1588 1792 (CP/M 3 is supplied in two versions.  One version supports nonbank-switched memory; the) 1792 SB
225 1647 1852 (second version supports hardware with bank-switched memory capabilities.  CP/M 3 supplies) 1852 SB
225 1706 1813 (additional facilities for the bank-switched system, including extended command line editing,) 1813 SB
225 1765 1165 (password protection of files, and extended error messages.) 1165 SB
375 1884 1765 (The nonbanked system requires 8.5 kilobytes of memory, plus space for your customized) 1765 SB
225 1943 1275 (BIOS.   It can execute in a minimum of 32 kilobytes of memory.) 1275 SB
375 2061 1783 (The bank-switched system requires a minimum of two memory banks with 11 kilobytes of) 1783 SB
225 2120 1948 (memory in Bank 0 and 1.5 kilobytes in common memory, plus space for your customized BIOS.   ) 1948 SB
225 2180 1609 (The bank-switched system provides more user memory for application programs.) 1609 SB
375 2298 1729 (CP/M 3 resides in the file CPM3.SYS, which is loaded into memory by a system loader) 1729 SB
225 2357 1915 (during system initialization.  The system loader resides on the first two tracks of the system disk.) 1915 SB
225 2416 1392 (CPM3.SYS contains the distributed BDOS and the customized BIOS.) 1392 SB
375 2535 1797 (The CP/M 3 operating system is distributed on two single- density, single-sided, eight-inch) 1797 SB
225 2594 1879 (floppy disks.  Digital Research supplies a sample BIOS that is configured for an Altos 8000-15) 1879 SB
225 2653 1770 (microcomputer system with bank-switched memory and two single- density, single-sided,) 1770 SB
225 2712 575 (eight-inch floppy disk drives.) 575 SB
1188 2890 25 (1) 25 SB
