225 227 754 (     1.2 CP/M 3 System Components) 754 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 345 1779 (          The CP/M 3 operating system consists of the following three modules: the Console) 1779 SB
225 405 1826 (Command Processor \(CCP\), the Basic Disk Operating System \(BDOS\), and the Basic Input) 1826 SB
225 464 472 (Output System \(BIOS\).) 472 SB
225 582 1946 (          The CCP is a program that provides the basic user interface to the facilities of the operating) 1946 SB
225 641 1926 (system.  The CCP supplies six built- in commands: DTR, DIRS, ERASE, RENAME, TYPE, and) 1926 SB
225 700 1940 (USER.  The CCP executes in the Transient Program Area \(TPA\), the region of memory where all) 1940 SB
225 760 1890 (application programs execute.       The CCP contains the Program Loader Module, which loads) 1890 SB
225 819 1416 (transient \(applications\) programs from disk into the TPA for execution.) 1416 SB
225 937 1813 (          The BDOS is the logical nucleus and file system of CP/M 3. The BDOS provides the) 1813 SB
225 996 1865 (interface between the application program and the physical input/output routines of the BIOS.) 1865 SB
225 1115 1795 (          The BIOS is a hardware-dependent module that interfaces the BDOS to a particular) 1795 SB
225 1174 1912 (hardware environment.  The BIOS performs all physical I/O in the system.     The BIOS consists) 1912 SB
225 1233 1861 (of a number of routines that you must configure to support the specific hardware of the target) 1861 SB
225 1292 350 (computer system.) 350 SB
225 1410 1810 (          The BDOS and the BIOS modules cooperate to provide the CCP and other transient) 1810 SB
225 1470 1731 (programs with hardware-independent access to CP/M 3 facilities.  Because the BIOS is) 1731 SB
225 1529 1936 (configured for different hardware environments and the BDOS remains constant, you can transfer) 1936 SB
225 1588 1887 (programs that run under CP/M 3 unchanged to systems with different hardware configurations.) 1887 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1706 875 (     1.3 Communication Between Modules) 875 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1825 1947 (          The BIOS loads the CCP into the TPA at system cold and warm start.  The CCP moves the) 1947 SB
225 1884 1851 (Program Loader Module to the top of the TPA and uses the Program Loader Module to load) 1851 SB
225 1943 384 (transient programs.) 384 SB
225 2061 1822 (          The BDOS contains a set of functions that the CCP and applications programs call to) 1822 SB
225 2120 1109 (perform disk and character input and output operations.) 1109 SB
225 2239 1821 (          The BIOS contains a Jump Table with a set of 33 entry points that the BDOS calls to) 1821 SB
225 2298 1862 (perform hardware-dependent primitive functions, such as peripheral device I/O.  For example,) 1862 SB
225 2357 1756 (CONIN is an entry point of the BIOS called by the BDOS to read the next console input) 1756 SB
225 2416 196 (character.) 196 SB
1188 2890 25 (2) 25 SB
225 92 654 (1.2 CP/M 3 System Components) 654 SB
1728 92 447 (CP/M 3 System Guide) 447 SB
