225 1625 1273 (               Figure 1-1.  General Memory Organization of CP/M 3) 1273 SB
225 1803 1867 (          Note that all memory regions in CP/M 3 are page aligned,   which means that they must) 1867 SB
225 1862 1829 (begin on a page boundary.  Because a page is defined as 256 \(100H\) bytes, a page boundary) 1829 SB
225 1921 1823 (always begins at a hexadecimal address where the low-order byte of the hex address is zero.) 1823 SB
