225 405 1890 (             In the banked system, the BDOS and the BIOS are separated into two parts: a resident) 1890 SB
225 464 1885 (portion, and a banked portion.  The resident BDOS and BIOS are located in common memory.) 1885 SB
225 523 1895 (The banked BDOS and BIOS are located in the operating system bank, referred to as Bank 0 in) 1895 SB
225 582 238 (this manual.) 238 SB
225 700 1792 (             The TPA extends from 100H in Bank 1 up to the bottom of the resident BDOS in) 1792 SB
225 760 1903 (common memory.  The banked BIOS and BDOS reside in Bank 0 with the directory buffers.     ) 1903 SB
225 819 1887 (Typically, all data buffers reside in common.  Data buffers  can reside in an alternate bank if the) 1887 SB
225 878 1895 (system has a DMA controller   capable of transferring arbitrary blocks of data from one bank to) 1895 SB
225 937 1822 (another.  Hashed directory tables \(one per drive\) can be placed    in any bank except Bank 1) 1822 SB
225 996 1350 (\(TPA\). Hashed directory tables require   4 bytes per directory entry.) 1350 SB
