0 0 0 fC
225 227 1891 (           Digital Research supplies a CP/M 3 loader file, CPMLDR, which you can link with your) 1891 SB
225 286 1915 (customized loader BIOS and use to load the CPM3.SYS file into memory.  CPMLDR is a small,) 1915 SB
225 345 1833 (self-contained version of CP/M 3 that supports only console output and sequential file input.) 1833 SB
225 405 1872 (Consistent with CP/M 3 organization, it contains two modules: an invariant CPMLDR BDOS,) 1872 SB
225 464 1832 (and a variant CPMLDR-BIOS, which is adapted to match the host microcomputer hardware) 1832 SB
225 523 1894 (environment. The CPMLDR BIOS module can perform cold start initialization of I/O ports and) 1894 SB
225 582 1941 (similar functions.  CPMLDR can display a memory map of the CP/M 3 system at start-up.  This is) 1941 SB
225 641 397 (a GENCPM option.) 397 SB
225 760 1814 (           The following steps tell you how to create a new version of CP/M 3 tailored to your) 1814 SB
225 819 360 (specific hardware.) 360 SB
225 937 198 (           1\) ) 198 SB
525 937 1617 (Write and assemble a customized BIOS following the specif ications described in ) 1617 SB
525 996 1446 (Section 3.   This software module must correspond to the exact physical ) 1446 SB
525 1055 1478 (characteristics of the target system, including memory and port addresses, ) 1478 SB
525 1115 833 (peripheral types, and drive characteristics.) 833 SB
225 1233 185 (           2\)) 185 SB
525 1233 1504 ( Use the system generation utility, GENCPM, to create the CPM3.SYS file ) 1504 SB
525 1292 1453 (containing the CP/M 3 distributed BDOS and your customized BIOS, as ) 1453 SB
525 1351 450 (described in Section 5.) 450 SB
225 1470 198 (           3\) ) 198 SB
525 1470 1632 (Write a customized loader BIOS \(LDRBIOS\) to reside on the system tracks as of ) 1632 SB
525 1529 1583 (CPMLDR.  CPMLDR loads the CPM3.SYS file into memory from disk.           ) 1583 SB
525 1588 1560 (Section 5 gives the instructions for customizing the LDRBIOS and generating ) 1560 SB
525 1647 1584 (CPMLDR.    Link your customized LDRBIOS file with the supplied CPMLDR ) 1584 SB
525 1706 74 (file.) 74 SB
225 1825 185 (           4\)) 185 SB
525 1825 1492 ( Use the COPYSYS utility to put CPMLDR on the system tracks of a disk.) 1492 SB
225 1943 198 (           5\) ) 198 SB
525 1943 1041 (Test and debug your customized version of CP/M 3.) 1041 SB
225 2061 1765 (           If you have banked memory, Digital Research recommends that you first use your) 1765 SB
225 2120 1929 (customized BIOS to create a nonbanked version of the CP/M 3 operating system.  You can leave) 1929 SB
225 2180 1917 (your entire BIOS in common memory until you have a working system.  Test all your routines in) 1917 SB
225 2239 1351 (a nonbanked version of CP/M 3 before you create a banked version.) 1351 SB
