683 674 1035 (                         Figure 2-1.  CP/M 3 System Tracks) 1035 SB
225 792 1839 (              The cold start procedure is designed so you need to initialize the system tracks only) 1839 SB
225 851 1896 (once.  This is possible because the system tracks contain the system loader and need not change) 1896 SB
225 911 1887 (when you change the CP/M 3 operating system.  The Cold Start Loader loads CPMLDR into a) 1887 SB
225 970 1899 (constant memory location that is chosen when the system is configured.    However , CPMLDR) 1899 SB
225 1029 1887 (loads the BDOS and BIOS system components into memory as specified in the CPM3.SYS file) 1887 SB
225 1088 1945 (generated by GENCPM, the system generation utility.  Thus, CP/M 3 allows the user to configure) 1945 SB
225 1147 1881 (a new system with GENCPM and then run it without having to update the system tracks of the) 1881 SB
225 1206 242 (system disk.) 242 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1325 495 (         2.4 Character I/O) 495 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1443 1904 (              CP/M 3 assumes that all simple character I/O operations are performed in 8-bit ASCII,) 1904 SB
225 1502 1931 (upper- and lowercase, with no parity.  An ASCII CRTL-Z \(lAH\) denotes an end-of-file condition) 1931 SB
225 1561 384 (for an input device.) 384 SB
225 1680 1276 (              Table 2-4 lists the characteristics of the logical devices.) 1276 SB
