225 1055 766 (         3.1 The System  Control Block) 766 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1174 1882 (              The System Control Block \(SCB\) is a data structure located in the BDOS.   The SCB) 1882 SB
225 1233 1884 (contains flags and data used by the CCP, the BDOS, the BIOS,  and other system components.) 1884 SB
225 1292 1862 (The BIOS can access specif ic data   in the System Control Block through the public variables) 1862 SB
225 1351 1418 (defined in the SCB.ASM file, which is supplied on the distribution disk.) 1418 SB
225 1470 1788 (              Declare the variable names you want to reference in the SCB as externals in your) 1788 SB
225 1529 1470 (BIOS.ASM source file.  Then link your BIOS with the SCB.REL module.) 1470 SB
225 1647 1856 (              In the SCB.ASM file, the high-order byte of the various SCB addresses is defined as) 1856 SB
225 1706 1927 (0FEH.  The linker marks absolute external equates as page relocatable when generating a System) 1927 SB
225 1765 1941 (Page Relocatable \(SPR\) format file.  GENCPM recognizes page relocatable addresses of 0FExxH) 1941 SB
225 1825 1897 (as references to the System Control Block in the BDOS.  GENCPM changes these addresses to) 1897 SB
225 1884 1385 (point to the actual SCB in the BDOS when it is relocating the system.) 1385 SB
225 2002 1910 (              Do not perform assembly-time arithmetic on any references to the external labels of the) 1910 SB
225 2061 1826 (SCB.  The result of the arithmetic could alter the page value to something other than 0FEH.) 1826 SB
225 2180 1904 (              Listing 3-1 shows the SCB.ASM file.  The listing shows the f ield names of the System) 1904 SB

