225 1174 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 1174 1618 (@BNKBF contains the address of a 128 byte buffer in the resident portion of the ) 1618 SB
525 1233 1542 (BDOS in a banked system.  This buffer is available for use during BOOT and ) 1542 SB
525 1292 1622 (WBOOT only.  You can use it to transfer a copy of the CCP from an image in an ) 1622 SB
525 1351 1241 (alternate bank if the system does not support interbank moves.) 1241 SB
225 1470 1454 (              @CRDMA, @FX, @USRCD, @ERDSK \(Read-Only Variable\)) 1454 SB
225 1588 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 1588 1579 (These variables contain the current DMA address, the BDOS function number, ) 1579 SB
525 1647 1508 (the current user code, and the disk code of the drive on which the last error ) 1508 SB
525 1706 1529 (occurred.     They can be displayed when a BDOS error is intercepted by the ) 1529 SB
525 1765 427 (BIOS.  See ?ERJMP.) 427 SB
225 1884 833 (              @CRDSK \(Read-Only Variable\)) 833 SB
225 2002 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 2002 1297 (@CRDSK is the current default drive, set by BDOS Function 14.) 1297 SB
