977 227 446 (Table 3-1. \(continued\)) 446 SB
225 345 492 (          Field       Meaning) 492 SB
225 464 830 (          @MLTIO    \(Read-Write Variable\)) 830 SB
225 582 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 582 1519 (@MLTIO contains the current multisector count. The BIOS can change the ) 1519 SB
525 641 1518 (multisector count directly, or through BDOS Function 44.  The value of the ) 1518 SB
525 700 852 (multisector count can range from 1 to 128.) 852 SB
225 819 791 (          @ERMDE \(Read-Only Variable\)) 791 SB
225 937 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 937 1611 (@ERMDE contains the current BDOS error mode. 0FFH indicates the BDOS is ) 1611 SB
525 996 1545 (returning error codes to the application program without displaying any error ) 1545 SB
525 1055 1555 (messages.  0FEH indicates the BDOS is both displaying and returning errors.  ) 1555 SB
525 1115 1552 (Any other value indicates the BDOS is displaying errors without notifying the ) 1552 SB
525 1174 425 (application program. ) 425 SB
225 1292 796 (          @MEDIA \(Read-Write Variable\)) 796 SB
225 1410 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 1410 1550 (@MEDIA is global system flag indicating that a drive door has been opened.  ) 1550 SB
525 1470 1573 (The BIOS routine that detects the open drive door sets this flag to 0FFH.  The ) 1573 SB
525 1529 127 (BIOS ) 127 SB
675 1529 1294 (routine also sets the MEDIA byte in  the Disk Parameter Header ) 1294 SB
525 1588 907 (associated with the open-door drive to 0FFH.) 907 SB
225 1706 770 (          @BFLGS \(Read-Only Variable\)) 770 SB
225 1825 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 1825 1487 (The BDOS in CP/M 3 produces two kinds of error messages:   short error ) 1487 SB
525 1884 1394 (messages and extended error messages.  Short error messages display ) 1394 SB
525 1943 1448 (one or two lines of text.  Long error messages display a third line of text ) 1448 SB
525 2002 1554 (containing the filename, filetype, and BDOS Function Number involved in the ) 1554 SB
525 2061 112 (error.) 112 SB
225 2180 1785 (                      In banked systems, GENCPM sets this flag in the System Control Block to ) 1785 SB
375 2239 1625 (indicate whether the BIOS displays short or extended error messages. Your error ) 1625 SB
375 2298 1627 (message handler should check this byte in the System Control Block.  If the high- ) 1627 SB
225 2357 1586 (order bit, bit 7, is set to 0, the BDOS displays short error messages. if the high- ) 1586 SB
225 2416 1568 (order bit is set to 1, the BDOS displays the extended three-line error messages.) 1568 SB
