225 582 273 (                     ) 273 SB
525 582 1588 (The ?ERJMP vector allows the BIOS to intercept the BDOS error messages so ) 1588 SB
525 641 1622 (you can display them in a foreign language.  Note that this vector is not branched ) 1622 SB
525 700 1643 (to if the application program is expecting return codes on physical errors. Refer to ) 1643 SB
375 760 1153 (the CP/M Plus Programmer's Guide for more information.) 1153 SB
225 878 273 (                     ) 273 SB
525 878 1641 (?ERJMP is set to point to the default \(English\) error message routine contained in ) 1641 SB
375 937 1614 (the BDOS. The BOOT routine can modify the address at ?ERJMP+L to point to ) 1614 SB
375 996 1544 (an alternate message routine.  Your error message handler can refer to @FX, ) 1544 SB
375 1055 1436 (@VINFO \(if @RESEL is equal to OFFH\), @CRDMA, @CRDSK, and ) 1436 SB
375 1115 1638 (@USRCD to print additional error information.  Your error handler should return ) 1638 SB
225 1174 1506 (to the BDOS with a RET instruction after printing the appropriate message.) 1506 SB
225 1292 803 (           @MXTPA \(Read-Only Variable\)) 803 SB
225 1410 273 (                     ) 273 SB
525 1410 1638 (@MXTPA contains the address of the current BDOS entry point.  This is also the ) 1638 SB
375 1470 1576 (address of the top of the TPA.  The BOOT and WBOOT routines of the BIOS ) 1576 SB
375 1529 1549 (must use this address to initialize the BDOS entry JMP instruction at location ) 1549 SB
375 1588 1541 (005H, during system initialization.  Each time a RSX is loaded, @MXTPA is ) 1541 SB
375 1647 1616 (adjusted by the system to reflect the change in the available User Memory \(TPA\).) 1616 SB
