225 1943 1926 (           TheBIOS data structure CHRTBL is a character table describing the physical I/O devices.) 1926 SB
225 2002 1896 (CHRTBL contains 6-byte physical device names and the characteristics of each physical device.) 1896 SB
225 2061 1905 (These characteristics include a mode byte, and the current baud rate, if any, of the device.    The) 1905 SB
225 2120 1848 (DEVICE utility references the physical devices through the names and attributes contained in) 1848 SB
225 2180 1749 (your CHRTBL. DEVICE can also display the physical names and characteristics in your) 1749 SB
225 2239 209 (CHRTBL.) 209 SB
225 2357 1904 (           The mode byte specifies whether the device is an input or output device, whether it has a) 1904 SB
225 2416 1753 (selectable baud rate, whether it is a serial device, and if XON/XOFF protocol is enabled.) 1753 SB
