675 464 1463 (allocation vectors, the user must type a CTRL-C at the system prompt to ) 1463 SB
225 523 307 (      \(continued\)) 307 SB
675 523 1366 (reset the disk system to ensure accurate reporting of free space.  Set ) 1366 SB
675 582 1380 (ALV to 0FFFEH for GENCPM to automatically assign space for the ) 1380 SB
675 641 1451 (allocation vector, single- or double-bit, during system generation.  In the ) 1451 SB
675 700 1497 (nonbanked system, GENCPM prompts for the type of allocation vector. In ) 1497 SB
525 760 1380 (the banked system, the allocation vector is always double-bit and can ) 1380 SB
525 819 1391 (reside in common memory or Bank 0. When GENCPM automatically ) 1391 SB
525 878 1427 (assigns space for the allocation vector \(ALV = OFFFEH\) , it places the ) 1427 SB
525 937 549 (allocation vector in Bank 0.) 549 SB
225 1055 406 (             DIRBCB    ) 406 SB
675 1055 1411 (Set DIRBCB to the address of a single directory Buffer Control Block ) 1411 SB
675 1115 1457 (\(BCB\) in an unbanked system. Set DIRBCB to the address of a BCB list ) 1457 SB
675 1174 493 (head in a banked system.) 493 SB
225 1292 299 (                       ) 299 SB
675 1292 1492 (Set DIRBCB to OFFFEH for GENCPM to set up the DIRBCB field.  The ) 1492 SB
675 1351 1336 (BDOS uses directory buffers for all accesses of the disk directory.  ) 1336 SB
525 1410 1451 (Several DPHs can refer to the same directory BCB or BCB list head; or, ) 1451 SB
525 1470 1340 (each DPH can reference an independent BCB or BCB list head.      ) 1340 SB
375 1529 1255 (Section 3.3.4 describes the format of the Buffer Control Block.) 1255 SB
225 1647 422 (             DTABCB    ) 422 SB
675 1647 1493 (Set DTABCB to the address of a single data BCB in an unbanked system.  ) 1493 SB
525 1706 1296 (Set DTABCB to the address of a data BCB list head in a banked ) 1296 SB
1875 1706 13 ( ) 13 SB
525 1765 148 (system.) 148 SB
225 1884 299 (                       ) 299 SB
675 1884 1322 (Set DTABCB to OFFFEH for GENCPM to set  up the DTABCB ) 1322 SB
2025 1884 125 ( field. ) 125 SB
675 1943 1463 (The BDOS uses data buffers  to hold physical sectors so that it can block ) 1463 SB
675 2002 1435 (and  deblock logical 128-byte records.  If the physical record size of the ) 1435 SB
675 2061 1481 (media associated with a DPH is 128 bytes, you can set the DTABCB field ) 1481 SB
675 2120 1432 (of the  DPH to 0FFFFH, because in this case, the BDOS does not use a ) 1432 SB
675 2180 228 (data buffer.) 228 SB
