225 464 317 (         HASH     ) 317 SB
675 464 1287 (Set RASH to OFFFEH to make directory hashing on the drive a ) 1287 SB
225 523 281 (    \(continued\)) 281 SB
675 523 1495 (GENCPM option. Each DPH   using hashing must reference a unique hash ) 1495 SB
525 582 1372 (table.    If a hash table is supplied, it must be 4*\(DRM+l\) bytes long, ) 1372 SB
525 641 1434 (where DRM is one less than the length of the directory. In other words, ) 1434 SB
525 700 1410 (the hash table    must contain four bytes for each directory entry of the ) 1410 SB
525 760 94 (disk.) 94 SB
225 878 344 (        HBANK     ) 344 SB
675 878 1478 (Set HBANK to the bank number of the hash table. HBANK is not used in ) 1478 SB
675 937 1366 (unbanked systems and should be set to zero.  The hash tables can be ) 1366 SB
675 996 1400 (contained in the system bank, common memory, or any alternate bank ) 1400 SB
675 1055 1393 (except Bank 1, because hash tables cannot be located in the Transient ) 1393 SB
675 1115 1488 (Program Area.   GENCPM automatically sets HBANK when HASH is set ) 1488 SB
525 1174 240 (to 0FFFEH.) 240 SB
