225 2002 1945 (             CP/M allocates disk space in a unit called a block.  Blocks are also called allocation units,) 1945 SB
225 2061 1950 (or clusters. BLS is the number of bytes in a block.  The block size can be 1024, 2048, 4096, 8192,) 1950 SB
225 2120 509 (or 16384 \(decimal\) bytes.) 509 SB
225 2239 1864 (             A large block size decreases the size of the allocation vectors but can result in wasted) 1864 SB
225 2298 1844 (disk space.  A smaller block size increases the size of the allocation vectors because there are) 1844 SB
225 2357 688 (more blocks on the same size disk.) 688 SB
225 2475 1883 (             There is a restriction on the block size.  If the block size is 1024, there cannot be more) 1883 SB
225 2535 1883 (than 255 blocks present on a logical drive.   In other words, if the disk is larger than 256K, it is) 1883 SB
225 2594 840 (necessary to use at least 2048 byte blocks.) 840 SB
225 2712 1934 (             The value of BLS is not a field in the Disk Parameter Block; rather, it is derived from the) 1934 SB
225 2771 932 (values of BSH and BLM as given in Table 3-4.) 932 SB
