225 227 1880 (              The DRM entry is one less than the total number of 32-byte directory entries, and is a) 1880 SB
225 286 1917 (16-bit value.  DRM must be less than or equal to \(BLS/32 * 16\) - 1. DRM determines the values) 1917 SB
225 345 1902 (of AL0 and ALI.  The two fields AL0 and ALI can together be considered a string of 16 bits, as) 1902 SB
225 405 412 (shown in Figure 3-4.) 412 SB
936 770 527 (Figure 3-4.  ALO and ALI) 527 SB
225 947 1888 (              Position 00 corresponds to the high-order bit of the byte labeled AL0, and position 15) 1888 SB
225 1006 1920 (corresponds to the low-order bit of the byte labeled ALI.  Each bit position reserves a data block) 1920 SB
225 1066 1898 (for a number of directory entries, thus allowing a maximum of 16 data blocks to be assigned for) 1898 SB
225 1125 1930 (directory entries.  Bits are assigned starting at 00 and filled to the right until position 15.       AL0) 1930 SB
225 1184 1913 (and ALI overlay the first two bytes of the allocation vector for the associated drive.     Table 3-6) 1913 SB
225 1243 1034 (shows DRM maximums for the  various block sizes.) 1034 SB
