225 1953 1907 (              If DRM = 127 \(128 directory entries\) ,  and BLS = 1024, there are 32 directory entries) 1907 SB
225 2012 1939 (per block, requiring 4 reserved blocks.  In this case, the 4 high-order bits of AL0 are set, resulting) 1939 SB
225 2071 1824 (in the values AL0 = OF0H and AL1 = 00H.  The maximum directory allocation is 16 blocks) 1824 SB
225 2131 1070 (where the block size is determined by BSH and BLM.) 1070 SB
225 2249 1898 (              The OFF field determines the number of tracks that are skipped at the beginning of the) 1898 SB
225 2308 1842 (physical disk.    It can be used as a mechanism for skipping reserved operating system tracks,) 1842 SB
225 2367 1873 (which on system disks contain the Cold Boot Loader, CPMLDR, and possibly the CCP.    It is) 1873 SB
225 2426 1311 (also used to partition a large disk into smaller segmented sections.) 1311 SB
