225 819 408 (               REC#       ) 408 SB
675 819 1463 (Identifies the record position of the current contents of the buffer located ) 1463 SB
675 878 1479 (at address BUFFAD.  REC# consists of the absolute sector number of the ) 1479 SB
675 937 1047 (record where the first record of the directory is zero.) 1047 SB
225 1055 425 (               WFLG       ) 425 SB
675 1055 1435 (Set by the BDOS to OFFH to indicate that the buffer contains new data ) 1435 SB
675 1115 1482 (that has not yet been written to disk.  When the data is written, the BDOS ) 1482 SB
675 1174 1245 (sets the WFLG to zero to indicate the buffer is no longer dirty.) 1245 SB
225 1292 362 (               00         ) 362 SB
675 1292 570 (Scratch byte used by BDOS.) 570 SB
225 1410 1727 (               TRACK      Contains the physical track location of the contents of the buffer.) 1727 SB
225 1529 1785 (               SECTOR     Contains  the physical sector location of the contents  of the buffer.) 1785 SB
225 1647 1638 (               BUFFAD    Specifies the address of the buffer associated with this BCB.) 1638 SB
225 1765 412 (               BANK      ) 412 SB
675 1765 1428 (Contains the bank number of the buffer associated with this BCB.  This ) 1428 SB
675 1825 769 (field is only present in banked systems.) 769 SB
225 1943 404 (               LINK       ) 404 SB
675 1943 1460 (Contains the address of the next BCB in a linked list, or zero if this is the ) 1460 SB
675 2002 1369 (last BCB in the linked list.  The LINK field is present only in banked ) 1369 SB
675 2061 167 (systems.) 167 SB
225 2180 1842 (               The BDOS   distinguishes between two kinds of buffers: data buffers referenced by) 1842 SB
225 2239 1906 (DTABCB, and directory buffers referenced by DIRBCB.  In a banked system, the DIRBCB and) 1906 SB
225 2298 1890 (DTABCB fields of a Disk Parameter Header each contain the address of a BCB list head rather) 1890 SB
225 2357 1910 (than the address of an actual BCB.  A BCB list head is a word containing the address of the first) 1910 SB
225 2416 1909 (BCB in a linked list.  If several DPHs reference the same BCB list, they must reference the same) 1909 SB
225 2475 1916 (BCB list head.  Each BCB has a LINK field that contains the address of the next BCB in the list,) 1916 SB
225 2535 547 (or zero if it is the last BCB.) 547 SB
