225 227 1947 (         In banked systems, the one-byte BANK field indicates the bank in which the data buffers are) 1947 SB
225 286 1835 (located.  The BANK field of directory BCBs must be zero because directory buffers must be) 1835 SB
225 345 1926 (located in Bank 0, usually below the banked BDOS module, or in common memory.  The BANK) 1926 SB
225 405 1874 (field is for systems that support direct memory-to-memory transfers from one bank to another.) 1874 SB
225 464 1061 (\(See the BIOS XMOVE entry point in section 3.4.4.\)) 1061 SB
225 582 1923 (         The BCD data structures in a banked system must reside in Bank 0 or in common memory.) 1923 SB
225 641 1823 ( The buffers of data BCBs can be located in any bank except Bank I \(the Transient Program) 1823 SB
225 700 126 (Area\).) 126 SB
225 819 1818 (         For banked systems that do not support interbank block moves through XMOVE, the) 1818 SB
225 878 1928 (BANK field must be set to 0 and the data buffers must reside in common memory.  The directory) 1928 SB
225 937 1628 (buffers can be in Bank 0 even if the system does not support bank-to-bank moves.) 1628 SB
225 1055 1920 (         In the nonbanked system, the DPH, DIRBCB, and DTABCB can point to the same BCB if) 1920 SB
225 1115 1872 (the DPH defines a fixed media device.   For devices with removable media, the DPH DIRBCB) 1872 SB
225 1174 1897 (and the DPH DTABCB must reference different BCBS.  In banked systems, the DPH DIRBCB) 1897 SB
225 1233 949 (and DTABCB must point to separate list heads.) 949 SB
225 1351 1913 (         In general, you can enhance the performance of CP/M 3 by allocating more BCBS, but the) 1913 SB
225 1410 1453 (enhancement reduces the amount of TPA memory in nonbanked systems.) 1453 SB
225 1529 1940 (         If you set the DPH DIRBCB or the DPH DTABCB fields to 0FFFEH, the GENCPM utility) 1940 SB
225 1588 1943 (creates BCBS, allocates physical record buffers, and sets these f ields to the address of the BCBS.) 1943 SB
225 1647 1546 (This allows you to write device drivers without regard to buffer requirements.) 1546 SB
