225 227 349 (     SKEW Macro) 349 SB
225 345 1819 (           The SKEW macro generates a skew table and requires the following parameters: the) 1819 SB
225 405 1889 (number of physical sectors per track, the skew factor, and the first sector number on each track) 1889 SB
225 464 317 (\(usually 0 or 1\).) 317 SB
225 582 871 (           The form of the SKEW macro call is) 871 SB
225 641 831 (               label: SKEW       ?secs,?skf,?fsc) 831 SB
225 760 200 (     where:) 200 SB
225 819 311 (               ?secs ) 311 SB
675 819 850 (is the number of physical sectors per track;) 850 SB
225 878 327 (               ?skf    ) 327 SB
675 878 497 (is the sector skew factor;) 497 SB
225 937 324 (               ?fsc    ) 324 SB
675 937 785 (is the first sector number on each track.) 785 SB
