225 1351 306 (     DPB Macro) 306 SB
225 1470 1937 (           The DPB macro generates a Disk Parameter Block specifying the characteristics of a drive) 1937 SB
225 1529 1902 (type.  It requires six parameters: the physical sector size in bytes, the number of physical sectors) 1902 SB
225 1588 1802 (per track, the total number of tracks on the drive, the size of an allocation unit in bytes, the) 1802 SB
225 1647 1901 (number of directory entries desired, and the number of system tracks to reserve at the beginning) 1901 SB
225 1706 1946 (of the drive.  There is an optional seventh parameter that defines the CKS field in the DPB.  If this) 1946 SB
225 1765 1525 (parameter is missing, CKS is calculated from the directory entries parameter.) 1525 SB
225 1884 828 (           The form of the DPB macro call is) 828 SB
225 1943 1306 (               label:   DPB    ?psize,?pspt,?trks,?bls,?ndirs,?off[,?ncks]) 1306 SB
225 2061 200 (     where:) 200 SB
225 2120 355 (               ?psize   ) 355 SB
675 2120 690 (is the  physical sector size in bytes;) 690 SB
225 2180 352 (               ?pspt    ) 352 SB
675 2180 863 (is the  number of physical sectors per track;) 863 SB
225 2239 344 (               ?trks    ) 344 SB
675 2239 730 (is the  number of tracks on the drive;) 730 SB
225 2298 336 (               ?bls     ) 336 SB
675 2298 679 (is the  allocation unit size in bytes;) 679 SB
225 2357 352 (               ?ndirs   ) 352 SB
675 2357 683 (is the  number of directory entries;) 683 SB
225 2416 337 (               ?off     ) 337 SB
675 2416 690 (is the  number of tracks to reserve;) 690 SB
225 2475 358 (               ?ncks    ) 358 SB
675 2475 858 (is the  number of checked directory entries.) 858 SB
225 2594 1833 (           The following example shows the parameters for a standard single-density disk drive:) 1833 SB
225 2712 1011 (               DPB$SD: DPB       128,26,77,1024,64,2) 1011 SB
