225 819 1943 (              This section defines the BIOS system initialization routines BOOT, WBOOT, DEVTBL,) 1943 SB
225 878 495 (DEVINI, and DRVTBL.) 495 SB
225 1055 906 (                               BIOS Function 0: BOOT) 906 SB
225 1174 1033 (                        Get Control from Cold Start Loader) 1033 SB
225 1233 827 (                                and Initialize System) 827 SB
225 1351 882 (                               Entry Parameters: None) 882 SB
225 1470 909 (                               Returned Values:    None) 909 SB
225 1588 1774 (              The BOOT entry point gets control from the Cold Start Loader in Bank 0 and is) 1774 SB
225 1647 1911 (responsible for basic system initialization.  Any remaining hardware initialization that is not done) 1911 SB
225 1706 1917 (by the boot ROMS, the Cold Boot Loader, or the LDRBIOS should be performed by the BOOT) 1917 SB
225 1765 154 (routine.) 154 SB
225 1884 1794 (              The BOOT routine must perform the system initialization outlined in Section 2.3,) 1794 SB
225 1943 1947 ("System Initialization." This includes initializing Page Zero jumps and loading the CCP.      BOOT) 1947 SB
225 2002 1912 (usually prints a sign-on message, but this can be omitted.  Control is then transferred to the CCP) 1912 SB
225 2061 429 (in the TPA at 0100H.) 429 SB
225 2180 1949 (              To initialize Page Zero, the BOOT routine must place a jump at location 0000H to BIOS) 1949 SB
225 2239 1942 ( base + 3, the BIOS warm start entry point. The BOOT routine must also place a jump instruction) 1942 SB
225 2298 1856 (at location 0005H to the address contained in the System Control Block variable, @MXTPA.) 1856 SB
225 2416 1814 (              The BOOT routine must establish its own stack area if it calls any BDOS or BIOS) 1814 SB
225 2475 1890 (routines.  In a banked system, the stack is in Bank 0 when the Cold BOOT routine is entered.   ) 1890 SB
225 2535 924 (The stack must be placed in common memory.) 924 SB
