225 227 913 (                         BIOS Function  1:   WBOOT) 913 SB
225 345 1075 (                    Get Control When a  Warm Start Occurs) 1075 SB
225 464 817 (                          Entry Parameters: None) 817 SB
225 582 844 (                          Returned Values:    None) 844 SB
225 700 1909 (         The WBOOT entry point is entered when a warm start occurs.  A warm start is performed) 1909 SB
225 760 1895 (whenever a user program branches to location 0000H or attempts to return to the CCP.      The) 1895 SB
225 819 1877 (WBOOT routine must perform the system initialization outlined in BIOS Function 0, including) 1877 SB
225 878 982 (initializing Page zero jumps and loading the CCP.) 982 SB
225 996 1862 (         When your WBOOT routine is complete, it must transfer control to the CCP at location) 1862 SB
225 1055 379 (0100H in the TPA.) 379 SB
225 1174 1874 (         Note that the CCP does not reset the disk system at warm start. The CCP resets the disk) 1874 SB
225 1233 1279 (system when a CTRL-C is pressed following the system prompt.) 1279 SB
225 1351 1899 (         Note also that the BIOS stack must be in common memory to make BDOS function calls.) 1899 SB
225 1410 1458 (Only the BOOT and WBOOT routines can perform BDOS function calls.) 1458 SB
225 1529 1932 (         If the WBOOT routine is reading the CCP from a file, it must set the multisector I/O count,) 1932 SB
225 1588 1833 (@MLTIO in the System Control Block, to the number of 128-byte records to be read in one) 1833 SB
225 1647 1909 (operation before reading CCP.COM. You can directly set @MLTIO in the SCB, or you can call) 1909 SB
225 1706 1179 (BDOS Function 44 to set the multisector count in the SCS.) 1179 SB
225 1825 1878 (         If blocking/deblocking is done in the BIOS instead of in the BDOS, the WBOOT routine) 1878 SB
225 1884 643 (must discard all pending buffers.) 643 SB
225 2061 914 (                         BIOS Function 20: DEVTBL) 914 SB
