225 523 1836 (          CP/M 3 assumes all simple character I/O operations are performed in eight-bit ASCII,) 1836 SB
225 582 1900 (upper and lowercase, with no parity. ANASCII CTRL-Z \(lAH\) denotes an end-of-file condition) 1900 SB
225 641 384 (for an input device.) 384 SB
225 760 1911 (          In CP/M 3, you can direct each of the five logical character devices to any combination of) 1911 SB
225 819 1897 (up to twelve physical devices. Each of the  five logical devices has a 16-bit vector in the System) 1897 SB
225 878 1717 (Control Block \(SCB\) . Each bit of the vector represents a physical device where bit 15) 1717 SB
225 937 1879 (corresponds to device zero, and bit 4 is device eleven.  Bits 0 through 3 are reserved for future) 1879 SB
225 996 227 (system use.) 227 SB
225 1115 1885 (          You can use the public names defined in the supplied SCB.ASM file to reference the I/O) 1885 SB
