225 1351 1825 (           SECTRN performs logical  sequential sector address to physical sector translation to) 1825 SB
225 1410 1920 (improve the overall response of CP/M 3. Digital Research ships standard CP/M disk with a skew) 1920 SB
225 1470 1840 (factor of 6, where six physical sectors are skipped between each logical read operation.  This) 1840 SB
225 1529 1912 (skew factor allows enough time between sectors for most programs on a slow system to process) 1912 SB
225 1588 1812 (their buffers without missing the next sector.  In computer systems that use fast processors,) 1812 SB
225 1647 1818 (memory, and disk subsystems, you can change the skew factor to improve overall response.) 1818 SB
225 1706 1807 (Typically, most disk systems perform well with a skew of every other physical sector.  You) 1807 SB
225 1765 1920 (should maintain support of single-density, IBM 3740 compatible disks using a skew factor of 6   ) 1920 SB
225 1825 1663 (in your CP/M 3 system to allow information transfer to and from other CP/M users.) 1663 SB
225 1943 1926 (           SECTRN receives a logical sector number in BC, and a translate table address in DE. The) 1926 SB
225 2002 1852 (logical sector number is relative to zero. The translate table address is obtained from the Disk) 1852 SB
225 2061 1891 (Parameter Block for the currently selected disk.  The sector number is used as an index into the) 1891 SB
225 2120 1727 (translate table, with the resulting physical sector number returned in HL.  For standard,) 1727 SB
225 2180 1891 (single-density, eight- inch disk systems, the tables and indexing code are provided in the sample) 1891 SB
225 2239 631 (BIOS and need not be changed.) 631 SB
225 2357 1933 (           Certain drive types either do not need skewing or perform the skewing externally from the) 1933 SB
225 2416 1823 (system software.  In this case, the skew table address in the DPH can be set to zero, and the) 1823 SB
225 2475 1823 (SECTRN routine can check for the zero in DE and return with the physical sector set to the) 1823 SB
225 2535 278 (logical sector.) 278 SB
