225 227 1870 (          You can place portions of the disk I/O routines in the system bank, Bank 0. In a banked) 1870 SB
225 286 1903 (environment, if the disk I/O hardware supports DMA transfers to and from banks other than the) 1903 SB
225 345 1803 (currently selected bank, the disk I/O drivers can reside in Bank 0. If the system has a DMA) 1803 SB
225 405 1821 (controller that supports block moves from memory to memory between banks, CP/M 3 also) 1821 SB
225 464 1933 (allows you to place the blocking and deblocking buffers in any bank other than Bank 1, instead of) 1933 SB
225 523 360 (common memory.) 360 SB
225 641 1947 (          If your disk controller supports data transfers only into the currently selected bank, then the) 1947 SB
225 700 1917 (code that initiates and performs a data transfer must reside in common memory.  In this case, the) 1917 SB
225 760 1908 (disk I/O transfer routines must select the DMA bank, perform the transfer, then reselect Bank 0.) 1908 SB
225 819 1334 (The routine in common memory performs the following procedure:) 1334 SB
225 937 1069 (          1\) Selects the DMA bank that SETBNK saved.) 1069 SB
225 996 631 (          2\) Performs physical I/O.) 631 SB
225 1055 539 (          3\) Reselects Bank 0.) 539 SB
225 1115 1356 (          4\) Returns to the calling READ or WRITE routine in Bank 0.) 1356 SB
225 1233 1849 (          Note that Bank 0 is in context \(selected\) when the BDOS calls the system initialization) 1849 SB
225 1292 1871 (functions BOOT and DRVTBL; the disk I/O routines HOME, SELDSK, SETTRK, SETSEC,) 1871 SB
225 1351 1864 (SETDMA, READ, WRITE, SECTRN, MULTIO, and FLUSH; and the memory management) 1864 SB
225 1410 659 (routines KMOVE and SETBNK.) 659 SB
225 1529 1826 (          Bank 0 or Bank 1 is in context when the BDOS calls the system initialization routines) 1826 SB
225 1588 1832 (WBOOT, DEVTBL, and DEVINI; the character I/O routines CONST, CONIN, CONOUT,) 1832 SB
225 1647 1937 (LIST, AUXOUT, AUXIN, LISTST, CONOST, AUXIST, and AUXOST, the memory select and) 1937 SB
