225 345 1805 (             This section assumes you have developed a BIOS3.ASM or BNKBIOS3.ASM file) 1805 SB
225 405 1913 (appropriate to your specific hardware environment. Use the Digital Research Relocatable Macro) 1913 SB
225 464 1861 (Assembler RMAC to assemble the BIOS.  Use the Digital Research Linker LINK-8   OTM to) 1861 SB
225 523 1830 (create the BIOS3.SPR and BNKBIOS3.SPR files.  The SPR files are part of the input to the) 1830 SB
225 582 403 (GENCPM program.) 403 SB
225 700 1849 (             In a banked environment, your CP/M 3 BIOS can consist of two segments: a banked) 1849 SB
225 760 1782 (segment and a common segment.  This allows you to minimize common memory usage to) 1782 SB
225 819 1907 (maximize the size of the TPA.  To prepare a banked BIOS, place code and data that must reside) 1907 SB
225 878 1850 (in common in the CSEG segment, and code and data that can reside in the system bank in the) 1850 SB
225 937 1939 (DSEG segment.  When you link the BIOS, LINK-80 creates the BNKBIOS3.SPR file with all the) 1939 SB
225 996 1139 (CSEG code and data first, then the DSEG code and data.) 1139 SB
225 1115 1885 (             After assembling the BIOS with RMAC, link your BNKBIOS using LINK-80 with the) 1885 SB
225 1174 1863 ([B] option.  The [B] option aligns the DSEG on a page boundary, and places the length of the) 1863 SB
225 1233 915 (CSEG into the BNKBIOS3.SPR header page.) 915 SB
225 1351 1941 (             Use the following procedure to prepare a BIOS3.SPR or BNKBIOS3.SPR file from your) 1941 SB
225 1410 365 (customized BIOS.) 365 SB
