225 585 1909 (               This section discusses the modular organization of the example CP/M 3 BIOS on your) 1909 SB
225 644 1753 (distribution disk.  For previous CP/M operating systems, it was necessary to generate all) 1753 SB
225 703 1914 (input/output drivers from a single assembler source file.   Such a file is difficult to maintain when) 1914 SB
225 762 1912 (the BIOS supports several peripherals.  As a result, Digital Research is distributing the BIOS for) 1912 SB
225 821 664 (CP/M 3 in several small modules.) 664 SB
225 940 1918 (               The organization of the BIOS into separate modules allows you to write or modify any) 1918 SB
225 999 1921 (I/O driver independently of the other modules.  For example, you can easily add another disk I/O) 1921 SB
225 1058 1600 (driver for a new controller with minimum impact on the other parts of the BIOS.) 1600 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1177 987 (         4.1 Functional Sumary of BIOS Modules) 987 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1295 1696 (               The modules of the BIOS are BIOSKRNL.ASM, SCB.ASM, BOOT.ASM,) 1696 SB
225 1354 1894 (MOVE.ASM, CHARIO.ASM, DRVTBL.ASM, and a disk I/O module for each supported disk) 1894 SB
225 1413 607 (controller in the configuration.) 607 SB
225 1531 1745 (               BIOSKRNL.ASM is the kernel, root, or supervisor module of the BIOS.  The) 1745 SB
225 1591 1795 (SCB.ASM module contains references to locations in the System Control Block.  You can) 1795 SB
225 1650 1921 (customize the other modules to support any hardware configuration.  To customize your system,) 1921 SB
225 1709 1609 (add or modify external modules other than the kernel and the SCE.ASM module.) 1609 SB
225 1827 1837 (               Digital Research supplies the BIOSKRNL.ASM module.  This module is the fixed,) 1837 SB
225 1886 1844 (invariant portion of the BIOS, aiid the interface from the BDOS to all BIOS functions.    It is) 1844 SB
225 1946 1860 (supplied in source form for reference only, and you should not modify it except for the equate) 1860 SB
225 2005 941 (statement described in the following paragraph.) 941 SB
225 2123 1687 (               You must be sure the equate statement \(banked equ true\) at the start of the) 1687 SB
225 2182 1752 (BIOSKRNL.ASM source file is correct for your system configuration.  Digital Research) 1752 SB
225 2241 1815 (distributes the BIOSKRNL.ASM file for a banked system.  If you are creating a BIOS for a) 1815 SB
225 2301 1294 (nonbanked system, change the equate statement to the following:) 1294 SB
225 2419 564 (                  banked equ false) 564 SB
225 2478 13 ( ) 13 SB
225 2537 1910 (and reassemble with RMAC.  This is the only change you should make to the BIOSKRNL.ASM) 1910 SB
225 2596 74 (file.) 74 SB
225 2715 1317 (               Table 4-1 summarizes the modules in the CP/M 3 BIOS.) 1317 SB
