225 878 1898 (              The Digital Research RMAC relocating assembler and LINK-80 linkage editor allow a) 1898 SB
225 937 1868 (module to reference a symbol contained in another module by name.  This is called an external) 1868 SB
225 996 1857 (reference.  The Microsoft relocatable object module format that RMAC and LINK use allows) 1857 SB
225 1055 1930 (six-character names for externally defined symbols.  External names must be declared PUBLIC in) 1930 SB
225 1115 1813 (the module in which they are defined.  The external names must be declared EXTRN in any) 1813 SB
225 1174 575 (modules that reference them.) 575 SB
225 1292 1904 (              The modular BIOS defines a number of external names for specific purposes.  Some of) 1904 SB
225 1351 1928 (these are defined as public in the root module, BIOSKRNL.ASM. Others are declared external in) 1928 SB
225 1410 1696 (the root and must be defined by the system implementor.  Section 4.4 contains a table) 1696 SB
225 1470 1432 (summarizing all predefined external symbols used by the modular BIOS.) 1432 SB
225 1588 1864 (              External names can refer to either code or data.  All predefined external names in the) 1864 SB
225 1647 1924 (modular BIOS prefixed with  a @ character refer to data items.  All external names prefixed with) 1924 SB
225 1706 1821 (a ? character refer to a code label.  To prevent conflicts with future extensions, user-defined) 1821 SB
225 1765 1018 (external names should not contain these characters.) 1018 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1884 687 (        4.3 Interactions of Modules) 687 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 2002 1848 (              The root module of the BIOS, BIOSKRNL.ASM, handles all BDOS calls, performs) 1848 SB
225 2061 1552 (interfacing functions, and simplifies the individual modules you need to create.) 1552 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 2180 462 (        4.3.1 Initial Boot) 462 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 2298 1649 (              BIOSKRNL.ASM initializes all configured devices in the following order:) 1649 SB
225 2416 1541 (              1\) BIOSKRNL calls ?CINIT in the CHARIO module for each of the) 1541 SB
225 2475 1153 (                 16 character devices and initializes the devices.) 1153 SB
225 2594 1496 (              2\) BIOSKRNL invokes the INIT entry point of each XDPH in the) 1496 SB
225 2653 621 (                 FD1797SD module.) 621 SB
