225 227 1066 (                     Table 4-6.  BOOT Module Entry Points) 1066 SB
225 345 795 (          Module                          Meaning) 795 SB
225 464 395 (          ?INIT           ) 395 SB
675 464 1312 (The BIOSKRNL module calls ?INIT during cold start to perform ) 1312 SB
675 523 1452 (hardware initialization other than character and disk I/O.   Typically, this ) 1452 SB
675 582 1426 (hardware can include time-of-day clocks, interrupt systems, and special ) 1426 SB
675 641 665 (I/O ports used for bank selection.) 665 SB
225 760 350 (          ?LDCCP   ) 350 SB
675 760 1392 (BIOSKRNL calls ?LDCCP during cold start to load the CCP into the ) 1392 SB
675 819 1435 (TPA.  The CCP can be loaded either from the system tracks of the boot ) 1435 SB
675 878 1410 (device or from a file, at the discretion of the system implementor.  In a ) 1410 SB
675 937 1394 (banked system, you can place a copy of the CCP in a reserved area of ) 1394 SB
675 996 1307 (another bank to increase the performance of the ?RLCCP routine.) 1307 SB
225 1115 1893 (          ?RLCCP          BIOSKRNL calls ?RLCCP during warm start to reload the CCP into the ) 1893 SB
675 1174 1476 (TPA.  In a banked system, the CCP can be copied from an alternate bank  ) 1476 SB
675 1233 1465 (to eliminate any disk access.   Otherwise, the CCP should be loaded from ) 1465 SB
675 1292 1125 (either the system tracks of the boot device or from a file.) 1125 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1470 430 (    4.6 Character I/O) 430 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1588 1815 (          The CHARIO module handles all character device interfacing. The CHARIO module) 1815 SB
225 1647 1802 (contains the character device definition table @CTBL, the character input routine ?CI , the) 1802 SB
225 1706 1833 (character output routine ?CO, the character input status routine ?CIST, the character output) 1833 SB
225 1765 1528 (status routine ?COST, and the character device initialization routine ?CINIT.) 1528 SB
225 1884 1872 (          The BIOS root module, BIOSKRNL.ASM, handles all character I/O redirection.    This) 1872 SB
225 1943 1769 (module determines the appropriate devices to perform operations and executes the actual) 1769 SB
225 2002 1693 (operation by calling ?CI, ?CO, ?CIST, and ?COST with the proper device number\(s\).) 1693 SB
225 2120 1840 (          @CTBL is the external name for the structure CHRTBL described in Section 3 of this) 1840 SB
225 2180 1889 (manual.  @CTBL contains an 8-byte entry for each physical device def-ined by this BIOS.  The) 1889 SB
225 2239 1041 (table is terminated by a zero byte after the last entry.) 1041 SB
225 2357 1833 (          The first field of the character device table, @CTBL, is the 6- byte device name.  This) 1833 SB
225 2416 1798 (device name should be all upper-case, left- justified, and padded with ASCII spaces \(20H\).) 1798 SB
