225 227 1003 (                      Table 4-9.  Character Device Labels) 1003 SB
225 345 491 (          Label      Meaning) 491 SB
225 464 725 (          ?Ci     Character Device Input) 725 SB
225 582 273 (                     ) 273 SB
675 582 1395 (?CI is called with a device number in register B. It should wait for the ) 1395 SB
675 641 1482 (next available input character , then return the character in register A. The ) 1482 SB
525 700 987 (character should be in 8-bit ASCII with no parity.) 987 SB
225 819 784 (          ?CO     Character Device Output) 784 SB
225 937 273 (                     ) 273 SB
675 937 1333 (?CO is called with a device number in register B and a character in ) 1333 SB
525 996 1347 (register C. It should wait until the device is ready to accept another ) 1347 SB
375 1055 1492 (character and then send the character. The character is in 8-bit ASCII with ) 1492 SB
225 1115 190 (no parity.) 190 SB
225 1233 900 (          ?CIST   Character Device Input Status) 900 SB
225 1351 273 (                     ) 273 SB
675 1351 1444 (?CIST is called with a device number in register B. It should return with ) 1444 SB
675 1410 1460 (register A set to zero if the device specified has no input character ready; ) 1460 SB
675 1470 1452 (and should return with A set to 0FFH if the device specified has an input ) 1452 SB
675 1529 530 (character ready to be read.) 530 SB
225 1647 954 (          ?COST   Character Device Output Status) 954 SB
225 1765 273 (                     ) 273 SB
675 1765 1463 (?COST is called with a device number in register B. It should return with ) 1463 SB
675 1825 1392 (register A set to zero if the device specified cannot accept a character ) 1392 SB
675 1884 1445 (immediately, and should return with A set to 0FFH if the device is ready ) 1445 SB
675 1943 426 (to accept a character.) 426 SB
225 2061 903 (          ?CINIT Character Device Initialization) 903 SB
225 2180 273 (                     ) 273 SB
675 2180 1428 (?CINIT is called for each of the 16 character devices, and initializes the ) 1428 SB
675 2239 1400 (devices.  Register C contains the device number.  The ?CINIT routine ) 1400 SB
675 2298 1460 (initializes the physical character device specified in register C to the baud ) 1460 SB
675 2357 1493 (rate contained in the appropriate entry of the CHRTBL.  You only need to ) 1493 SB
525 2416 1290 (supply this routine if I/O redirection has been implemented.  It is ) 1290 SB
525 2475 1225 (referenced only by the DEVICE utility supplied with CP/M 3.) 1225 SB
