225 227 1145 (      4.7.3 Extended Disk Parameter Headers \(XDPHS\)) 1145 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 345 1839 (            An Extended Disk Parameter Header \(XDPH\) consists of a prefix and a regular Disk) 1839 SB
225 405 1827 (Parameter Header as described in Section 3. The label of a XDPH references the start of the) 1827 SB
225 464 1623 (DPH.  The fields of the prefix are located at relative offsets from the XDPH label.) 1623 SB
225 582 1946 (            The XDPHs for each unit of a controller are the only entry points in a particular disk drive) 1946 SB
225 641 1945 (module.  They contain both the DPH for the drive and the addresses of the various action routines) 1945 SB
225 700 1882 (for that drive, including READ, WRITE, and initialization.  Figure 4-1 shows the format of the) 1882 SB
225 760 678 (Extended Disk Parameter Header.) 678 SB
930 2673 540 (Figure 4-1.  XDPH Format) 540 SB
