225 227 1633 (              Table 4-10 describes the fields of each Extended Disk Parameter Header.) 1633 SB
225 345 1038 (                           Table 4-10.  Fields of Each XDPH) 1038 SB
225 464 817 (              Field                            Meaning) 817 SB
225 582 405 (              WRITE     ) 405 SB
675 582 1449 (The WRITE word contains the address of the sector WRITE routine for ) 1449 SB
675 641 187 (the drive.) 187 SB
225 760 356 (              READ   ) 356 SB
675 760 1477 (The READ word contains the address of the sector READ routine for the ) 1477 SB
675 819 113 (drive.) 113 SB
225 937 389 (              LOGIN    ) 389 SB
675 937 1383 (The LOGIN word contains the address of the LOGIN routine for the ) 1383 SB
675 996 113 (drive.) 113 SB
225 1115 1942 (              INIT            The INIT word contains the address of the f irst-time initialization code for ) 1942 SB
525 1174 187 (the drive.) 187 SB
225 1292 1863 (              UNIT            The UNIT byte contains the drive code relative to the disk controller.  ) 1863 SB
675 1351 1446 (This is the value placed in @RDRV prior to calling the READ, WRITE, ) 1446 SB
675 1410 741 (and LOGIN entry points of the drive.) 741 SB
225 1529 1942 (              TYPE            The TYPE byte is unused by the BIOS root, and is reserved for the driver ) 1942 SB
525 1588 1463 (to keep the current density or media type to support multiple-format disk ) 1463 SB
525 1647 235 (subsystems.) 235 SB
225 1765 1744 (           regular DPH     The remaining fields of the XDPH comprise a standard DPH, as ) 1744 SB
675 1825 742 (discussed in Section 3 of this manual.) 742 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 2002 753 (         4.7.4 Subroutine Entry Points) 753 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 2120 1849 (              The pointers contained in the XDPH reference the actual code entry points to a disk) 1849 SB
225 2180 1830 (driver module.  These routines are not declared public.  Only the XDPH itself is public.  The) 1830 SB
225 2239 1790 (BIOS root references the XDPHs only through the @DTBL.  Table 4-11 shows the BIOS) 1790 SB
225 2298 470 (subroutine entry points.) 470 SB
