225 227 993 (                    Table 4-11.  Subroutine Entry Points) 993 SB
225 345 823 (          Entry Point                       meaning) 823 SB
225 464 431 (             WRITE        ) 431 SB
675 464 1464 (When the WRITE routine is called, the address of the XDPH is passed in ) 1464 SB
675 523 1454 (registers DE.  The parameters for the WRITE operation are contained in ) 1454 SB
675 582 1351 (the public variables @ADRV, @RDRV, @TRK, @SECT, @DMA,) 1351 SB
225 641 338 (                          ) 338 SB
675 641 1477 (and @DBNK. The WRITE routine should return an error code in register ) 1477 SB
675 700 1490 (A. The code 00 means a successful operation, 01 means a permanent error ) 1490 SB
525 760 1362 (occurred, and 02 means the drive is write-protected if that feature is ) 1362 SB
525 819 212 (supported.) 212 SB
225 937 1922 (             READ         When the READ routine is called, the address of the XDPH is contained in ) 1922 SB
675 996 1431 (registers DE.  The parameters for the READ operation are contained in ) 1431 SB
675 1055 1448 (the public variables @ADRV, @RDRV, @TRK, @SECT, @DMA, and ) 1448 SB
675 1115 1492 (@DBNK.  The READ routine should return an error code in register A. A ) 1492 SB
525 1174 1464 (code of 00 means a successful operation and 01 means a permanent error ) 1464 SB
525 1233 189 (occurred.) 189 SB
225 1351 1840 (             LOGIN        The LOGIN routine is called before the BDOS logs into the drive, and ) 1840 SB
675 1410 1435 (allows the automatic determination of density.  The LOGIN routine can ) 1435 SB
675 1470 1370 (alter the various parameters in the DPH, including the translate table ) 1370 SB
675 1529 1461 (address \(TRANS\) and the Disk Parameter Block \(DPB\) .     The LOGIN ) 1461 SB
675 1588 1415 (routine can also set the TYPE byte.  On single media type systems, the ) 1415 SB
675 1647 1440 (LOGIN routine can simply return.  When LOGIN is called, the registers ) 1440 SB
675 1706 739 (DE point to the XDPH for this drive.) 739 SB
225 1825 387 (             INIT         ) 387 SB
675 1825 1373 (The BOOT entry of the BIOSKRNL module calls each INIT routine ) 1373 SB
675 1884 1454 (during  cold start and prior to any other disk accesses. INIT can perform ) 1454 SB
675 1943 1480 (any necessary hardware initialization, such as setting up the controller and ) 1480 SB
525 2002 478 (interrupt vectors, if any.) 478 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 2180 844 (    4.7.5    Error Handling and Recovery) 844 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 2298 1791 (          The READ and WRITE routines should perform several retries of an operation that) 1791 SB
225 2357 1905 (produces an error. If the error is related to a seek operation or a record not found condition, the) 1905 SB
225 2416 1911 (retry routine can home or restore the drive, and then seek the correct track.  The exact sequence) 1911 SB
225 2475 656 (of events is hardware-dependent.) 656 SB
