225 227 1888 (             When a nonrecoverable error occurst the READ or WRITE routines can print an error) 1888 SB
225 286 1880 (message informing the operator of the details of the error.  The BIOSKRNL module supplies a) 1880 SB
225 345 1848 (subroutine, ?PDERR, to print a standard BIOS error message header.  This routine prints the) 1848 SB
225 405 381 (following message:) 381 SB
225 523 741 (                BIOS Err on D: T-nn S-nn) 741 SB
225 641 1907 (        The D: is the selected drive, and T-nn and S-nn display the track and sector number for the) 1907 SB
225 700 1873 (operation.  The READ and WRITE routines should print the exact cause of the error after this) 1873 SB
225 760 1925 (message, such as Not Ready, or Write Protect.  The driver can then ask the operator if additional) 1925 SB
225 819 1438 (retries are desired, and return an error code to the BDOS if they are not.) 1438 SB
225 937 1836 (             However, if the @ERMDE byte in the System Control Block indicates the BDOS is) 1836 SB
225 996 1817 (returning error codes to the application program without printing error messages, the BIOS) 1817 SB
225 1055 1016 (should simply return an error without any message.) 1016 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1174 634 (        4.7.6 Multiple Sector I/O) 634 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1292 1789 (             The root module global variable @CNT contains the multisector count.   Refer to) 1789 SB
225 1351 1728 (Sections 2.5 and 3.4.3 for a discussion of the considerations regarding multirecord I/O.) 1728 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
225 1470 513 (        4.8 MOVE Module) 513 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 1588 1805 (             The MOVE Module performs memory-to-memory block moves and controls bank) 1805 SB
225 1647 1802 (selection.   The ?MOVE and ?XMOVE entry points correspond directly to the MOVE and) 1802 SB
225 1706 1884 (XMOVE jump vector routines documented in Section 3. Table 4-12 shows the entry points for) 1884 SB
225 1765 394 (the MOVE module.) 394 SB
