225 286 1325 (     CP/M 3 Sytem Guide                                  4.8 MOVE Module) 1325 SB
225 405 1071 (                     Table 4-12.  Move Module Entry Points) 1071 SB
225 523 570 (        Entry Point     Meaning) 570 SB
225 641 813 (        ?MOVE Memory-to-memory move) 813 SB
225 760 312 (                        ) 312 SB
675 760 1478 (?MOVE is called with the source address for the move in register DE, the ) 1478 SB
675 819 1435 (destination address in register HL, and the byte count in register BC.  If ) 1435 SB
675 878 1381 (?XMOVE has been called since the last call to ?MOVE, an interbank ) 1381 SB
675 937 1456 (move must be performed.  On return, registers HL and DE must point to ) 1456 SB
675 996 1327 (the next bytes after the MOVE. This routine can use special DMA ) 1327 SB
675 1055 1429 (hardware for the interbank move capability, and can use the Z8O LDIR ) 1429 SB
675 1115 634 (instruction for intrabank moves.) 634 SB
225 1233 1051 (        ?XMOVE Set banks for one following ?MOVE) 1051 SB
225 1351 312 (                        ) 312 SB
675 1351 1459 (?XMOVE is called with the destination bank in register B and the source ) 1459 SB
675 1410 1462 (bank in register C. Interbank moves are only invoked if the DPHs specify ) 1462 SB
675 1470 1438 (deblocking buffers in alternate banks. ?XMOVE only applies to one call ) 1438 SB
675 1529 938 (to ?MOVE. \(Not implemented in the example.\)) 938 SB
225 1647 726 (        ?BANK Set bank for execution) 726 SB
225 1765 312 (                        ) 312 SB
675 1765 1469 (?BANK is called with the bank address in register A.    This bank address ) 1469 SB
675 1825 1398 (has already been stored in @CBNK for future reference. All registers  ) 1398 SB
675 1884 833 (except A must be maintained upon return.) 833 SB
