997 345 406 (System Generation) 406 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 582 1773 (              This section describes the use of the GENCPM utility to create a memory image) 1773 SB
225 641 1844 (CPM3.SYS file containing the elements of the CP/M 3 operating system.     This section also) 1844 SB
225 700 1846 (describes customizing the LDRBIOS portion of the CPMLDR program, and the operation of) 1846 SB
225 760 1785 (CPMLDR to read the CPM3.SYS file into memory.        Finally, this section describes the) 1785 SB
225 819 749 (procedure to follow to boot CP/M 3. ) 749 SB
225 937 1911 (              In the nonbanked system, GENCPM creates the CPM3.SYS file from the BDOS3.SPR) 1911 SB
225 996 1833 (and your customized BIOS3.SPR files.  In the banked system, GENCPM creates the CPM3.) 1833 SB
225 1055 1842 (SYS f i le from the RESBDOS3.  SPR f i le, the BNKBDOS3.SPR file, and your customized) 1842 SB
225 1115 432 (BNKBIOS3.SPR file.) 432 SB
225 1233 1943 (              If your BIOS contains a segment that can reside in banked memory, GENCPM separates) 1943 SB
225 1292 1896 (the code and data in BNKBIOS3.SPR into a banked portion which resides in Bank 0 just below) 1896 SB
225 1351 1508 (common memory, and a resident portion which resides in common memory.) 1508 SB
225 1470 1802 (              GENCPM relocates the system modules, and can allocate physical record buffers,) 1802 SB
225 1529 1943 (allocation vectors, checksum vectors, and hash tables as requested in the BIOS data structures.  It) 1943 SB
225 1588 1801 (also relocates references to the System Control Block, as described on page 27. GENCPM) 1801 SB
225 1647 1775 (accepts its command input from a file, GENCPM.DAT, or interactively from the console.) 1775 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
