225 1174 1888 (           GENCpm determines the location of the system modules in memory and, optionally, the) 1888 SB
225 1233 1939 (number of physical record buffers allocated to the system.    GENCPM can specify the location of) 1939 SB
225 1292 1804 (hash tables requested by the Disk Parameter Headers \(DPHS\) in the BIOS.  GENCPM can) 1804 SB
225 1351 1900 (allocate all required disk buffer space and create all the required Buffer Control Blocks \(BCBs\).) 1900 SB
225 1410 1342 (GENCPM can also create checksum vectors and allocation vectors.) 1342 SB
225 1529 1899 (           GENCPM can get its input from a file GENCPM.DAT. The values in the file replace the) 1899 SB
225 1588 1889 (default values of GENCPM.  If you enter the AUTO parameter in the command line GENCPM) 1889 SB
225 1647 1888 (gets its input from the file GENCPM.DAT and generates a new system displaying only its sign-) 1888 SB
225 1706 1886 (on and sign-off messages on the console.  If AUTO is specified and a GENCPM.DAT file does) 1886 SB
225 1765 1402 (not exist on the current drive, GENCPM reverts to manual generation.) 1402 SB
225 1884 1681 (           If you enter the AUTO DISPLAY parameter in the command line, GENCPM) 1681 SB
225 1943 1819 (automatically generates a new system and displays all questions on the console.     If AUTO) 1819 SB
225 2002 1897 (DISPLAY is specified and a GENCPM.DAT file does not exist on the current drive, GENCPM) 1897 SB
225 2061 1855 (reverts to manual generation.   If GENCPM is running in AUTO mode and an error occurs, it) 1855 SB
225 2120 1171 (reverts to manual generation and starts from the beginning.) 1171 SB
