225 227 1934 (          The CPMLDR requires a customized LDRBIOS to perform disk input and console output.) 1934 SB
225 286 1918 (The LDRBIOS is essentially a nonbanked BIOS. The LDRBIOS has the same JMP vector as the) 1918 SB
225 345 1862 (regular CP/M 3 BIOS.  The LDRBIOS is called only to perform disk reads \(READ\) from one) 1862 SB
225 405 1787 (drive, console output \(CONOUT\) for sign-on messages, and minimal system initialization.) 1787 SB
225 523 1928 (          The CPMLDR calls the BOOT entry point at the beginning of the LDRBIOS to allow it to) 1928 SB
225 582 1939 (perform any necessary hardware initialization.  The BOOT entry point should return to CPMLDR) 1939 SB
225 641 1903 (instead of loading and branching to the CCP, as a BIOS normally does.  Note that interrupts are) 1903 SB
225 700 1146 (not disabled when the LDRBIOS BOOT routine is called.) 1146 SB
225 819 1832 (          Test your LDRBIOS completely to ensure that it properly performs console character) 1832 SB
225 878 1877 (output and disk reads.  Check that the proper tracks and sectors are addressed on all reads and) 1877 SB
225 937 1097 (that data is transferred to the proper memory locations.) 1097 SB
225 1055 1819 (          You should assemble the LDRBIOS.ASM file with a relocatable origin of 0000H.     ) 1819 SB
225 1115 1623 (Assemble the LDRBIOS with RMAC to produce a LDRBIOS.REL file.  Link the) 1623 SB
225 1174 1767 (LDRBIOS.REL file with the CPMLDR.REL file supplied by Digital Research to create a) 1767 SB
225 1233 1919 (CPMLDR.COM .file. Use the L option in LINK to specify the load origin \(address\) to which the) 1919 SB
225 1292 1236 (boot loader on track 0 sector 1 loads the CPMLDR.COM file.) 1236 SB
225 1410 1927 (          Unnecessary BIOS functions can be deleted from the LDRBIOS to conserve space.  There) 1927 SB
225 1470 1911 (is one absolute restriction on the length of the LDRBIOS; it cannot extend above the base of the) 1911 SB
225 1529 1929 (banked portion of CP/M 3.  \(GENCPM lists the base address of CP/M 3 in its load map.\)   If you) 1929 SB
225 1588 1916 (plan to boot CP/M 3 from standard, single-density, eight-inch floppy disks, your CPMLDR must) 1916 SB
225 1647 1883 (not be longer than 1980H to place the CPMLDR.COM file on two system tracks with the boot) 1883 SB
225 1706 1876 (sector.  If the CCP resides on the system tracks with the Cold Start Loader and CPMLDR, the) 1876 SB
225 1765 845 (combined lengths must not exceed 1980H.) 845 SB
