225 2357 1886 (          CPMLDR loads the CP/M 3 system file CPM3.SYS into Bank 0 and transfers control to) 1886 SB
225 2416 1822 (the BOOT routine in the customized BIOS.  You can specify in GENCPM for CPMLDR to) 1822 SB
225 2475 1564 (display a load table containing the names and addresses of the system modules.) 1564 SB
225 2594 1722 (          The CPM3.SYS file contains the CP/M 3 BDOS and customized BIOS. The file) 1722 SB
225 2653 1929 (CPM3.SYS must be on drive A in USER 0.   You can execute CPMLDR under SID  or DDT  to) 1929 SB
225 2712 1949 (help debug the BIOS.   A $B in the default File Control Block \(FCB\) causes CPMLDR to execute) 1949 SB
225 2771 1803 (a RST 7 \(SID breakpoint\) just before jumping to the CP/M 3 Cold Boot BIOS entry point.) 1803 SB
