225 1825 1896 (               The CP/M 3 cold start operation loads the CCP, BDOS, and BIOS modules into their) 1896 SB
225 1884 1865 (proper locations in memory and passes control to the cold start entry point \(BIOS Function 0:) 1865 SB
225 1943 1933 (BOOT\) in the BIOS. Typically, a PROM-based loader initiates a cold start by loading sector 0 on) 1933 SB
225 2002 1853 (track I of the system tracks into memory and jumping to it. This first sector contains the Cold) 1853 SB
225 2061 1938 (Start Loader.  The Cold Start Loader loads the CPMLDR.COM program into memory and jumps) 1938 SB
225 2120 1913 (to it.  CPMLDR loads the CPM3.SYS file into memory and jumps to the +BIOS cold start entry) 1913 SB
225 2180 115 (point.) 115 SB
