525 2061 1564 (With the CP/M 3 system in the proper location, you can set passpoints in your ) 1564 SB
525 2120 1550 (BIOS.  Use the L command with the address specified as the beginning of the ) 1550 SB
525 2180 1566 (BIOS by the CPMLDR load table as shown in step 5 above.  This L command ) 1566 SB
525 2239 1606 (causes SID to display the BIOS jump vector which begins at that address.    The ) 1606 SB
525 2298 1597 (jump vector indicates the beginning address of each subroutine in the table.  For ) 1597 SB
525 2357 1518 (example, the first jump instruction in the example below is to the Cold Boot ) 1518 SB
