1086 227 227 (Apendix B) 227 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
968 345 464 (Auto-density Support) 464 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
225 464 1865 (              AUto-density support refers to the capability of CP/M 3 to support different types of) 1865 SB
225 523 1713 (media on a single drive.  For example, some floppy-disk drives accept single-sided and) 1713 SB
225 582 1816 (double-sided disks in both single-density and double-density formats.  Auto-density support) 1816 SB
225 641 1876 (requires that the BIOS be able to determine the current density when SELDSK is called and to) 1876 SB
225 700 1885 (subsequently be able to detect a change in disk format when the READ or WRITE routines are) 1885 SB
225 760 128 (called.) 128 SB
225 878 1947 (              To support multiple disk formats, the drivers BIOS driver must include a Disk Parameter) 1947 SB
225 937 1797 (Block \(DPB\) for each type of disk or include code to generate the proper DPB parameters) 1797 SB
225 996 1929 (dynamically.  In addition, the BIOS driver must determine the proper format of the disk when the) 1929 SB
225 1055 1937 (SELDSK entry point is called with register E bit 0 equal to 0 \(initial SELDSK calls\).  If the BIOS) 1937 SB
225 1115 1950 (driver cannot determine the format, it can return OOOOH in register pair HL to indicate the select) 1950 SB
225 1174 1868 (was not successful.  Otherwise, it must update the Disk Parameter Header \(DPH\) to address a) 1868 SB
225 1233 1748 (DPB that describes the current media, and return the address of the DPH to the BDOS. ) 1748 SB
225 1352 104 (        ) 104 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 46 /MSTT31c133 font
329 1351 130 ( Note:) 130 SB
32 0 0 50 50 0 0 1 45 /MSTT31c126 font
459 1352 1665 ( all subsequent SELDSK calls with register E bit 0 equal to 1, the BIOS driver must) 1665 SB
225 1411 1924 (continue to return the address of the DPH returned in the initial SELDSK call.  The value 0000H) 1924 SB
225 1471 1028 (is only a legal return value for initial SELDSK calls.) 1028 SB
225 1589 1939 (              After a driver's SELDSK routine has determined the format of a disk, the driver's READ) 1939 SB
225 1648 1842 (and WRITE routines assume this is the correct format until an error is detected. If an error is) 1842 SB
225 1707 1862 (detected and the driver determines that the media has been changed to another format, it must) 1862 SB
225 1766 1857 (return the value OFFH in register A and set the media flag in the System Control Block.  This) 1857 SB
225 1826 1932 (signals the BDOS that the media has changed and the next BIOS call to the drive will be an initial) 1932 SB
225 1885 1856 (SELDSK call.  Do not modify the drivers DPH or DPB until the initial SELDSK call is made.) 1856 SB
225 1944 1859 (Note that the BDOS can detect a change in media and will make an initial SELDSK call, even) 1859 SB
225 2003 1928 (though the BIOS READ and WRITE routines have not detected a disk format change. However,) 1928 SB
225 2062 1398 (the SELDSK routine must always determine the format on initial calls.) 1398 SB
225 2181 1929 (               A drive's Disk Parameter Header \(DPH\) has associated with it several uninitialized data) 1929 SB
225 2240 1883 (areas:  the allocation vector, the checksum vector, the directory hash table, and physical record) 1883 SB
225 2299 1830 (buffers.  The size of these areas is determined by DPB parameters. If space for these areas is) 1830 SB
225 2358 1903 (explicitly allocated in the BIOS, the DPB that requires the most space determines the amount of) 1903 SB
225 2417 1922 (memory to allocate. If the BIOS defers the allocation of these areas to GENCPM, the DPH must) 1922 SB
225 2476 1907 (be initialized to the DPB with the largest space requirements.   If one DPB is not largest in all of) 1907 SB
225 2536 1926 (the above categories, a false one must be constructed so that GENCPM allocates sufficient space) 1926 SB
225 2595 367 (for each data area.) 367 SB
